    <PackageReleaseNotes>
v2.2.2 — Correctness, safety, and compatibility hardening
• Fix the default single-ring startup failure caused by requesting 65,536 SQ entries.
• Keep in-flight SEND buffers pinned until their terminal CQE or ring shutdown.
• Serialize multishot receive data while PipeWriter backpressure is active.
• Retry ACCEPT/eventfd submissions after SQ-full and prevent send-loop busy spins.
• Route aborts through idempotent socket shutdown/close and generation-safe slot release.
• Preserve TCP half-close semantics so delayed responses cannot target recycled fd slots.
• Drain graceful TLS connection-close responses before socket shutdown; cover sequential and concurrent handshake churn.
• Bound copied multishot backpressure data with a shared per-ring memory budget.
• Never unmap ring memory after an unconfirmed IO-loop shutdown.
• Quarantine the fixed-file table if a kernel unregister update fails.
• Fail closed on unrecoverable CQ overflow instead of duplicating unknown operations.
• Populate peer/local endpoints, report ephemeral ports, and use unique public connection IDs.
• Default UnsafeInlineScheduling to false; explicit opt-in is still available.
• Validate transport options early and preserve exact multi-ring capacity/configuration.

v2.2.1 — Slot free-list: fixes high-c correctness + unlocks stronger wins
• Fix: per-listener connection-slot allocator now uses a pre-populated free-list
  (Stack&lt;int&gt;) instead of the pre-2.2.1 `connId % MaxConnections` modulo. The
  modulo policy silently aliased connIds to slot indices and overwrote live
  connections' slots once connId count exceeded MaxConnections, orphaning their
  recv/send-loop/fd and producing mass errors at connection counts &gt; MaxConnections.
  Default MaxConnections is now 16384 (was 1024). Slot release is deferred until
  all in-flight CQEs for the closing connection have drained, so the generation
  check correctly rejects stale CQEs instead of misrouting them to a new
  connection that happened to claim the same slot.
• Fix: HandleAccept now soft-rejects (close fd, log warning) when the free-list
  is empty, instead of the previous silent-overwrite. No more orphaning under
  bursts above MaxConnections.

